Glyphs must exist in the Google Noto font set.

1. The Vertical Axis: Voicing
Unvoiced Consonants: Sits on the baseline, has at least one ascender (no descenders).
Voiced Consonants: Has at least one descender (no ascenders).
Vowels: Stays entirely within the x-height (no ascenders, no descenders).

2. The Horizontal Axis: Place of Articulation
Front (Lips/Teeth): Asymmetrical, visually heavier on the left, points left.
Middle (Alveolar Ridge): Left-to-right symmetry.
Mid-Back (Postalveolar): Slightly asymmetrical, pointing mildly to the right.
Back (Palate/Velum/Glottis): Asymmetrical, visually heavier on the right, points right.

3. The Shape Axis: Manner of Articulation
Stops / Fricatives / Affricates: Kiki (sharp, angular, rigid). Stops are the most Kiki.
Nasals / Liquids / Glides: Bouba (rounded, curved, fluid). Nasals are the most Bouba.

4. The Vowel Space
Weight: All vowel glyphs are visually "bottom-heavy" (anchored/grounded), representing their fully voiced nature.
Focus: The visual focal point (an apex, a dot, or a point) maps to the vowel's coordinate on the IPA chart.
R-Coloring: Indicated by a terminal right-facing curl ) within the x-height.




